NimbyDpv (display name DPV) - original work by Jeff Fabish for NIMBY | HARDCORE | BADLANDS | 1pp:
config, scripts, model build pipeline, proxies, textures as derived, and the vehicle class NimbyDpv_Car.

Third-party model
-----------------
The vehicle mesh in data\dpv.p3d, data\dpvwheel.p3d and the texture set (data\dpv_*_co.paa, _nohq, _smdi
and their rvmats) are derived from "Desert Patrol Vehicle Low-poly 3D model" by carbuni, CGTrader
model 1875658 (https://www.cgtrader.com/3d-models/military/military-vehicle/desert-patrol-vehicle),
bought by Jeff Fabish on November 5, 2026 under CGTrader's Royalty Free License, "No AI" variant.
The purchase record is D:\DayZProjects\NimbyDpv\vendor-carbuni\LICENSE-NOTE.txt (not in the repository).

License read, November 8, 2026 (CGTrader General Terms and Conditions, Royalty Free License,
help.cgtrader.com article 360015124437):
- The license is limited to "Incorporated Product". A game counts when the model is contained inside
  a proprietary format and displayed during play; the buyer must take all reasonable measures to
  prevent the end user from gaining access to the product (the article names a proprietary product
  format, a protected resource file and encryption as examples). The model may not be sold, given
  or redistributed in the form it was downloaded, digital or printed.
- How this addon complies: the purchased OBJ, MAX, FLT, MB, MTL and PSD sources never enter a
  repository or a PBO (shared rules 9.3 exception, docs/design/dpv-feasibility.md D-2). What ships
  is a rebuilt, re-topologised game model (new LOD set, selections, memory points, proxies, skeleton,
  the NIMBY rail frame) binarized to Bohemia's ODOL format inside a signed PBO, with textures
  converted to PAA. An MLOD (editable) .p3d never ships in a release build; the MLOD files the
  builder writes are the local working copies only. Ruled November 5, 2026 (ship ODOL) and confirmed
  against the license November 8, 2026.
- Attribution is not required by the license; carbuni is credited here and in the Workshop text.
- "No AI": the model, its textures and anything derived from them are not to be used for machine
  learning training. The repository and the pack carry no such use.

Vanilla references
------------------
NimbyDpv_Car points at vanilla DayZ 1.30 (Bohemia Interactive) part, sound and material classes by
inheritance and name: the hatchback part set (CarBattery, SparkPlug, HeadlightH7, CarRadiator not
used), the Hatchback_02 engine sound set (config values copied from DZ/sounds/hpp/config.cpp, the
sound shaders themselves stay in the game data), vanilla rvmat conventions, and the model.cfg
animation sources. No vanilla model, texture or sound file is copied into the pack. The addon also
patches the inventorySlot[] lists of vanilla item classes (jerry can, ammo box, protector case,
scientific briefcase, first aid kit, Field Transceiver, wooden crate, teddy bear, three tents, the
Attack2Bag and eighteen backpack classes) so they can ride the DPV's rail, roof and cabin slots;
config only, nothing saved changes (Jeff, November 6, 2026, 23:08).

NimbyDpv_TestCar (Phase 0, November 5, 2026) is a config-only child of the vanilla OffroadHatchback
kept for the test harness; it reuses the vanilla model and parts through inheritance and copies
nothing.

